body:
Hi Paul - 

The method truncateHtml is protected which is why I am using truncate which has following signature:

string truncate( $string, $length, $suffix = '...', $encoding = null, $asHtml = false )

In my example above I have set the last parameter to True so checking the code I am actually using the truncateHtml one:

 public static function truncate($string, $length, $suffix = '...', $encoding = null, $asHtml = false)
{
if ($asHtml) {
return self::truncateHtml($string, $length, $suffix, $encoding ?: Yii::$app->charset);
}

I do think there is an error in the code somehwere. 
Let me know if you need more details.

Thank you

--Matt

You could hide the empty bullets

``` html
<style>
li:empty {
  display: none;
}
</style>
```

Also, If you purify the HTML `HTMLPufifier` should remove any empty elements.

OK I have a fix for the spaces issue, truncateHtml in the string helper seems to be adding spaces for no apparent reason, but fixing that, also forced me to fix the unit tests for it as they allow for the additional spaces. So I'll wait to see if the issue is confirmed before making a pull request.

current unit test

``` php
$this->assertEquals('<span>This is a test </span>...', StringHelper::truncate('<span>This is a test sentance</span>', 14, '...', null, true));
        $this->assertEquals('<span><img src="image.png" />This is a test </span>...', StringHelper::truncate('<span><img src="image.png" />This is a test sentance</span>', 14, '...', null, true));
```

'fixed' unit test

``` php
$this->assertEquals('<span>This is a test</span>...', StringHelper::truncate('<span>This is a test sentance</span>', 14, '...', null, true));
        $this->assertEquals('<span><img src="image.png" />This is a test</span>...', StringHelper::truncate('<span><img src="image.png" />This is a test sentance</span>', 14, '...', null, true));
```
